// SOURCE: NPC 'malchus'
// BIBLE REFERENCE: John 18:10–11; Luke 22:50–51; Matthew 26:52
// ------------------------------------------------------------
// PURPOSE: Malchus describes the arrest at Gethsemane — the violence and the healing
// ============================================================


-> start

=== start ===
I am the servant of the High Priest. We went to the garden to arrest the Nazarene. There was a scuffle, a flash of steel... and then a sharp pain in my ear.
* [Who struck you?] -> peter

=== peter ===
It was one of his followers, the one they call Peter. He drew a sword. But the Teacher rebuked him. He said, "Put your sword away! Shall I not drink the cup the Father has given me?"
* [Then what happened?] -> healing

=== healing ===
He touched my ear... and it was whole again. He healed me. The man we came to arrest, healed me. I... I don't understand.
-> DONE